-- title:
--   Diamond action on ℚ̄-points of the Pic⁰ model
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\neq 0$ with $5\le M$ and $p\nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a $\{p\}$-cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$, with $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$, and let $j\in K$, nonzero, whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Let $D$ be a `RelativePic0Designation` for the two-chart model [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, that is, a scheme $D.P$ with a structure morphism $D.\mathrm{toBase}$ to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$ and a section of it. Fix algebra structures making $A\to L\to\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ a tower. Assume given a bijection $\mathrm{gpts}$ between $J_1(Mp)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (degree-zero divisors modulo principal ones) and the morphisms $\mathrm{Spec}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, and a map $\varphi$ from the abstract Hecke algebra $\mathbb{Z}[X_i : i\in \mathrm{Primes}\sqcup\mathbb{N}]$ to endomorphisms of $D.P$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$, such that for the module structure [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleOneBar (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L129) one has $\mathrm{gpts}(t\cdot x)=\mathrm{gpts}(x)$ followed by $\varphi(t)$ for all $t$ and $x$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions. First, for every $d\in\mathbb{N}$ and every $y\in J_1(Mp)$, $\mathrm{gpts}$ of the image of $y$ under the semilinear automorphism $(\mathrm{diamondAutBar}(Mp,d),1)$ equals $\mathrm{gpts}(y)$ followed by $\varphi(X_{\mathrm{inr}\,d})$. Second, for every $d$, all places $P,Q$ of that function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and all degree-zero divisors $D_v,D_v'$ with $D_v=\delta_P-\delta_Q$ and $D_v'=\delta_{g\cdot P}-\delta_{g\cdot Q}$, where $g$ is the same semilinear automorphism, the class of $D_v'$ satisfies $\mathrm{gpts}([D_v'])=\mathrm{gpts}([D_v])$ followed by $\varphi(X_{\mathrm{inr}\,d})$.
--
--   This identifies the action of the diamond operator $\langle d\rangle$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points of the relative $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$ with transport of divisor classes along the diamond automorphism of the geometric function field, in the form needed on differences of places. It feeds the analysis of the special fibre of the Jacobian model and of the Atkin–Lehner and diamond conjugation relations used further on.
